        "evidence_id": "ev-0fed3501258bac9e",
        "path_or_url": "docs/source-continuation.md",
        "section": "Grounded partial answers and source continuation > Read only a missing part",
        "snippet": "## Read only a missing part\n\nWhen spare space remains in the initial 800-token admission budget, a selected\nproject source may carry `source_uri`. This optional locator never displaces a\nselected snippet. Pass the exact returned URI to MCP `resources/read`; ordinary\nMarkdown links are citations, not continuation capabilities. The initial response\nstill contains at most three sources and retains its public token-estimate meaning.",
        "version_binding": "unversioned",
        "content_sha256": "89d99acbd7fef7cf51bcfd99e1b99903fd88df9f78087324b13764ce2713c348",
        "project_identity": "git:github.com/Vanilla1999/DocAtlas",
        "authority": "source_of_truth",
        "scope": "module",
        "line_start": 16,
        "line_end": 22,
        "source_uri": "docatlas://source/dc211b86557cf39284c61340"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev-9c4e4bc207583e17",
        "path_or_url": "docs/grounded-host-session.md",
        "section": "Grounded host sessions over MCP > Partial answers and source reads",
        "snippet": "The host reads the returned snippets and assesses whether a requested fact is\nsupported. `support(fact_id, evidence_id=..., quote=...)` accepts only a verbatim\nquote from retained evidence. A matching quote binds the judgment to a source;\nit does not prove that the quote logically answers the question. Semantic\nassessment remains the host's responsibility.",
        "version_binding": "unversioned",
        "content_sha256": "51d4ac03bfd81bcaca873455dd1c81acf7ec6f79e96985c220eba0d19bb974ad",
        "project_identity": "git:github.com/Vanilla1999/DocAtlas",
        "authority": "source_of_truth",
        "scope": "module",
        "line_start": 16,
        "line_end": 20,
        "source_uri": "docatlas://source/fadece6e5ebad41f25925cf7"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "ev-d6821cc55bf2b657",
        "path_or_url": "docs/grounded-host-session.md",
        "section": "Grounded host sessions over MCP > Final handoff",
        "snippet": "`answer_supported` remains false in all three states. A read failure cannot turn\nan existing partial answer into an empty refusal. The host should state the\nsupported part, explicitly name what is unknown and provide a feasible next\nstep or a necessary clarifying question. Unknown private configuration is never\ninferred from a general documentation quote.",
        "version_binding": "unversioned",
        "content_sha256": "0bc5fe3a2c1cfd53fa893d9108ef24da0c8d5b0234c3ba47ecb21d6b7e012c58",
